[sub_resource type="Resource" id="Resource_2w7fw"]
script = ExtResource("36_jcrwi")
date = "8/9/1447"
text = "	There has been a notable shift in our community… I’ve never seen a bigger line when distributing food to the less fortunate. Much worse, the amount of bread our funds were able to purchase was far smaller than the regular portion. 

	It worries me, but our community is a strong and faithful one. The numbers at mass have been staggering, with people even having to sit on the floor, the pews overflowing with churchgoers. With crops dwindling, the people are eager to worship, hopeful that Faustine will grant us prosperity in this trying time. My fellow sisters have hardly left the statue, our knees raw and tender from praying. There are always people in the pews, lending their pleas as well. With this many prayers, Faustine will surely come to our aid."
metadata/_custom_type_script = "uid://cs8kccqb2huxb"

[sub_resource type="Resource" id="Resource_vamxk"]
script = ExtResource("36_jcrwi")
text = "	Even with us nuns praying nearly nonstop, our most devout worshipper may not be a nun at all, but the priest’s dear mother. An old, frail thing, but strong of heart and mind. She’s always been a regular churchgoer, but lately she’s been spending days praying in front of the statue with little time for breaks. Father Mason has requested that she be taken into our care; old as she is, she doesn’t need any more reason to fall ill, and this blossoming famine is making her extra susceptible. We are grateful to have her around–she’s a sweet old woman. I hope Faustine will value her many years of devotion, deeming her worthy of a blessing. She may be our greatest hope."
signature = "Sister Mira"
metadata/_custom_type_script = "uid://cs8kccqb2huxb"

