script = ExtResource("36_jcrwi")
date = "3/8/1447"
text = "	A curious thing occurred today as my sisters and I were cleaning up around the church. I had been scrubbing an exceptionally stubborn stain when the main hall doors swung open with great force. A panting, sweating man rushed in in a panic, his eyes wild. He clutched a plant in his hand, knuckles white around its thin stem. 

	“A great disaster” he proclaimed was coming as he waved the crop around frantically, the wild motion causing its colours to blur together. But when he stilled, I could see clearly the brown, thick scabs on its surface. Nasty, raised ridges, rough to the touch. A blight, he called it. And it wasn’t just this plant that it’d consumed. 

	He begged us to pray–pray as quickly and as deeply as we could, in hopes that Faustine might hear our pleas. I still don’t know what to make of it. Educated as I am, I don’t know much about farming, and this crazed man was hard to take seriously. Could it have just been some raving fool looking for attention? Could blemishes like this be a normal occurrence for crops?"
metadata/_custom_type_script = "uid://cs8kccqb2huxb"

[sub_resource type="Resource" id="Resource_kxak1"]
script = ExtResource("36_jcrwi")
text = "	Regardless, my sisters and I got to work praying, urging Faustine to protect us and lend us Her generosity. As I kneeled before the statue though, even in the shelter of Her might, I couldn’t shake the feeling of great dread… I hope to hear no more of this."
signature = "Sister Aubrey"
metadata/_custom_type_script = "uid://cs8kccqb2huxb"

